{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243317-post-apocalyptic-exalted","id":1243317,"title":"Post-apocalyptic Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-06T16:04:34-07:00","id":1243317,"title":"Post-apocalyptic Exalted","content":"I really like the post-apocalyptic elements of Exalted and want to emphasise things like weird cults and ways that mortals engage with the ruins and remnants of the First Age. I think early first edition especially, and third edition play up that vibe really well.<br /> <br /> For those of a similar mind, what visual/narrative elements have you used in your games / can you come up with along those lines?<br /> <br /> Starting it off...<ul><li>An urban gang with piece-meal, scavenged armour that's crudely bolted together, their leader wielding a battered, notched sword that bursts into flame at a command.</li> <li>A ancient library ran by a priesthood descended from the original librarians, their cataloging system now ritualised. Different sub-departments wage mini holy wars over informational minutiae and correct filing methods.</li> <li>The Temple of the Golden Steward: a church of baked mud and thatch crudely built into the side of a ruined mansion. Within sits a golden metal figure who wakes once a year, sparks of essence raining down from every joint as it slowly stands, tries to offer tea and cake from an empty tray to its worshipers in a dialect that none of them understand, then collapses once again, the light dimming from its crystal eyes.</li> <li>An aviary of beautiful clockwork birds, the size of a large palace, sits on a hill above the town. Flitting from sculpted trees, the birds sing beautifully. Residents of the town who are committed of serious crimes are thrown into the aviary where they are instantly flensed down to the bone.</li> <li>The sword of a warstrider, twenty feet high, is plunged into the bedrock near the docks of the city. Its huge, immovable, and so cold it fumes with steam. Enterprising townsfolk have built a warehouse around it, where they hang the carcasses of slaughtered livestock and other perishables. Every so often a hapless worker ignores warnings and touches the sword and is instantly flash frozen.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":1079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","user":"Megapope","date":". 08-06-2018, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T22:16:51-07:00","id":1243404,"title":"","content":"Y'know, in spite of it taking place in the mythic prehistory of our world, Robert E. Howard's Conan stories <i>also </i>took place after some cataclysmic catastrophes; for instance, the city-sized building he comes across in <i>Red Nails</i> had all its inhabitants die out a long time ago, long enough for a tribe to move in and settle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:08:32-07:00","id":1243476,"title":"","content":"You could hint at ancientness or fallen-ness by describing a few architectural styles. <br /> <br /> For instance, modern style in your setting might be all long buildings - whether proper longhouses or not. A few key hints might be efficiency of airflow and cooling if the long side faces into the prevailing wind and has an elevated roof; that you can hitch a large number of horses along the long side wall; that you can put two together (with a gap) and have half of a fenced work-yard already built; that it's easy security if you only have one entrance on a short side and a thief has to go through all of your retainers to steal your treasure. I'm thinking of a rural or small-town sort of feel, that's a sensory clue what civilization is like nowadays.<br /> <br /> A high-age style in the same setting might be all round and oval floor-plans, each with a dome, half-dome, or roof deck of some sort. You could hint at it with fallen columns while the (structurally resilient) round walls stand; that each was at one point surrounded by gardens and terraces, implying a lot of work just to get a basic home or common building set up; that each was designed to face a particular direction (a clue!) for a particular view. I'm thinking of a lost but once-wealthy civilization that had different priorities, placing importance on a particular aesthetic instead of practical utility. <br /> <br /> A low-age style could be heavily constructed, with large walls but tight overhangs and low ceilings. Unmarked danger holes leading downward for whatever purpose, and places where the floors between levels are opened up. The strategic purpose, or even the size &amp; shape of the occupants, might be hard to guess. Some good hints might be overgrowth, humidity, animal occupants, or strange scratches or partial markings. Throwing the sense of proportion out of whack could hint at a lost culture that's really ancient and weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T16:54:58-07:00","id":1243645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243317-post-apocalyptic-exalted?p=1243404#post1243404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, in spite of it taking place in the mythic prehistory of our world, Robert E. Howard's Conan stories <i>also </i>took place after some cataclysmic catastrophes; for instance, the city-sized building he comes across in <i>Red Nails</i> had all its inhabitants die out a long time ago, long enough for a tribe to move in and settle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically it's the fall of Atlantis, then the world's preeminent super power, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, make sure you have a really good reason why no one has moved in and &quot;civilized&quot; the place in the last 500 years since the Realm started. Some parts of Fallout stretch belief that no one has cleaned up old world tin cans in that games 200 years of surface life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}